WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.040
wrapping up the week on Tesla's short time, daily episode 501. Patrick here in Vancouver,

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:12.420
it's June 5th, 2026. Let's close out the week with today's Tesla news.

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:19.160
Tesla ending free supercharging for new Model 3's on June 15th removes a key ownership perk

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:26.780
just as buyers weigh total costs against rivals. Tesla expanded its unsupervised robotaxi operations

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:32.420
to cover the full Austin metro area. This more than doubles the previous service zone.

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:36.840
The change builds on limited testing that had been running in a smaller area.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:41.860
No details on fleet size or ride availability were released with the announcement.

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:48.640
The expansion positions Tesla ahead of broader regulatory decisions on unsupervised operations.

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:53.080
While robotaxi progress signals long-term autonomy bets,

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:57.260
leadership changes are also reshaping how those projects get executed.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:03.600
Tesla AI Infrastructure VP Raj Jiganath and left the company after 13 years.

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:10.120
He is moving to become CTO at Chrono Scale. The departure follows internal focus on fleet

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:15.560
utilization and expanding AI hardware needs across vehicle and robot programs.

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:21.340
No replacement has been named yet. This shift in leadership comes as Tesla balances

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:25.380
near-term product decisions with longer-term autonomy work.

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:31.420
Leadership shifts coincide with near-term product incentive changes that also affect how

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:38.020
customers value Tesla vehicles today. Tesla updated its configurator to show that the free supercharging

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:43.960
incentive for Model 3 Premium and Performance variants will stop after June 15th.

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:47.760
The change applies to new orders placed after that cutoff date.

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:54.200
Buyers who order before June 15th still receive lifetime free access at superchargers.

00:01:54.520 --> 00:02:00.760
The move comes as Tesla adjusts incentives while Model Y updates continue rolling out.

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:07.380
As incentives tighten, Tesla is simultaneously widening feature availability on existing models.

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:14.080
The base Model Y rear wheel drive and all wheel drive trims now ship with the 16-inch

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:19.880
center screen and black headliner. These were the version's formerly labeled standard range.

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:24.560
The update narrows the visible differences between entry and premium models.

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:30.460
Production changes appear to be rolling through current builds. These quick product tweaks reflect

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:35.540
the same manufacturing flexibility that the first principle segment explores later.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:41.900
JP Morgan raised its Tesla rating to neutral and lifted the price target to $475.

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:47.900
The upgrade sites Robotaxi and Optimus potential as primary long-term drivers.

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:53.260
It reverses the bank's prior bearish stance that had targeted significant downside.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:58.440
Analysts now see software and robotics as primary long-term drivers.

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:02.880
The new target implies roughly 13% upside from recent levels.

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:09.480
Analyst optimism on future software and robotics comes alongside fresh evidence of Tesla's global

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:17.180
sales momentum. Tesla cumulative UK sales crossed 300,000 units led by Model Y volume.

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:21.820
The milestone reflects steady growth despite limited local production.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:27.240
Registrations continue to outpace most rivals in the premium EV segment.

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:33.440
No specific quarterly breakdown was released with the announcement. Similar strength is appearing

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:40.660
in other export markets, including a sharp rebound in Japan. Tesla Japan deliveries rose 182%

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:48.260
year-over-year in May. Year-to-date growth reached 157%. Model Y accounted for the majority

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:53.680
of the increase after earlier price adjustments. The surge follows earlier price adjustments

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:59.320
and new inventory arrivals. Strong demand in Asia also shows up in South Korea,

00:03:59.320 --> 00:04:04.300
where Tesla holds the top imported EV spot for the fourth straight month.

00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:10.840
Tesla issued a recall covering 173 cyber trucks due to a potential wheel detachment,

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:16.560
linked to rotor components. The issue was identified during internal quality checks before

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:22.480
customer deliveries. Affected vehicles will receive inspections and replacements at service centers

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:29.200
at no cost. No customer incidents have been reported so far. Quality focus at scale is

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:34.580
one side of Tesla's production story. The other is how quickly the company can vary colors and

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:40.020
features without new hardware. There is a challenge worth discussing with the cyber truck recall.

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:47.420
Tesla is recalling 173 early units after internal checks found a rotor component that could

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:53.500
lead to wheeled attachment. The affected vehicles will be inspected and repaired at service centers

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:59.980
with no cost to owners. No customer reports of the issue have surfaced yet. The recall highlights

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:06.260
ongoing quality control focus as production scales. This approach shows how Tesla can catch and

00:05:06.260 --> 00:05:10.500
address issues early through factory checks rather than waiting for field reports.

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:16.520
Taking a step back from today's headlines, the sudden availability of coastal blue and the

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:23.220
expanded 16-inch screen on base model Y trims shows how quickly Tesla can alter visible product

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:29.520
details without new hardware platforms. Most automakers treat color and interior trim changes

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:36.320
as multi-year programs tied to major refreshes. Tesla's approach treats these elements as software

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:42.460
configurable options that can appear in the configurator within weeks. The result is a manufacturing

00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:49.580
system that decouples styling variety from structural engineering cycles. This flexibility rests on the

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:56.200
single shared body and interior architecture across trims. Adding a new paint or headliner color

00:05:56.200 --> 00:06:02.120
requires only supplier coordination and software updates rather than new tooling or assembly line

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:08.020
rebalancing. The same logic applies to the screen size change now reaching the former standard

00:06:08.020 --> 00:06:14.780
range models. Once the larger display and its mounting are validated on higher trims, propagating

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:21.360
it downward costs little marginal engineering effort. Data from earlier model 3 and Y refreshes

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:26.880
already demonstrated that such updates can be executed inside a single quarter. The practical

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:32.800
implication is that Tesla can respond to regional taste shifts or competitive pressure with far

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:39.700
lower fixed costs than rivals. Before we go, keep an eye on whether the Robotaxi Zone expansion leads

00:06:39.700 --> 00:06:46.420
to any new regulatory updates in the coming days. That's your Tesla news for today. TSLA closed at

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:57.960
$410.83, down $7.62, 1.8%. If you found this useful, a rating or review on Apple Podcast or Spotify

00:06:57.960 --> 00:07:03.980
really helps new listeners find the show. You can also find us on X at Tesla Shorts time.

